<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIAN KALEV EARNS MOST PROFIT FROM ESTONIA.</title>
<headline>ESTONIAN KALEV EARNS MOST PROFIT FROM ESTONIA.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's confectionary maker Kalev makes most of its profit from the domestic market although it exports over half of its production, chairman Tonis Allik said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The most imporant part of the profit comes from the domestic market,&quot; Allik said at the company's shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>Allik added that the company is forced to sell its production at lower prices in Russia, which is its most important export market, because Russia has imposed double tariffs on Estonian imports.</p>
<p>Kalev had a turnover of 321 million kroons in 1996, which is up from 238 million kroons in 1995. Its profit was 14.8 million kroons in 1996 compared to 7.5 million kroons the year before.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
